 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "609d3dc8-fb04-5b46-9d5c-0d04a9998ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469870} {:answer/id #uuid "22cf7953-1f96-59bb-b222-bec1a682923c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "609d3dc8-fb04-5b46-9d5c-0d04a9998ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469870} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fd438fe-248f-5b63-a47f-ff64630e73bb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1d4a0e7-8ceb-5003-89cd-d540839fd74d" :question/math-academy-id "q-96855" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,-1)$, $(1,0)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n- **I.** $(10,20)$\n- **II.** $(4,-8)$\n- **III.** $(-6,6)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -4 & 10 \\\\ -12 & -8 & 20\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,-12)$, $(-4,-8)$ and $(10,20).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I  only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049254 :topic/id #uuid "e6f9ad03-abe7-52d6-8a6a-acbcb8fbeef7" :topic/math-academy-id 1351 :topic/title "Singular Linear Transformations in the Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eab5693-da12-5573-98d2-914b3e12b5c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469872} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ff3136-e82c-5764-b831-f508f7cc961e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5eab5693-da12-5573-98d2-914b3e12b5c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469872} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb591b12-5ddd-5b7c-b516-9d0afdb7ff88" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470548} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbaf6140-9e34-5ed5-b8da-cd3527d54932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469874} {:answer/id #uuid "8576213b-ae76-5796-845c-f78bcab64b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8576213b-ae76-5796-845c-f78bcab64b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469875} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cd78585-b14a-5ede-9aac-0fb6d8a76426" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470549} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9548e387-0612-50a6-b2ce-c8aaf16214c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469876} {:answer/id #uuid "83c5b7ff-cf0f-5896-93c9-7248c571fa9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9548e387-0612-50a6-b2ce-c8aaf16214c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469876} :answer-field/id #uuid "a525d91f-6d56-5631-8b8d-6244e6dc1297" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b46e610-7522-5441-8d91-b874b0e467ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-96856" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,-1),(1,1),$ and $(3,2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(-1,4)$\n- **II.** $(-2,4)$\n- **III.** $(1,-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are  $(-2,4)$, and $(1,-2).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \" II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049254 :topic/id #uuid "e6f9ad03-abe7-52d6-8a6a-acbcb8fbeef7" :topic/math-academy-id 1351 :topic/title "Singular Linear Transformations in the Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9849851-50ee-5f0d-ab89-ef7a2fc9f84c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469878} {:answer/id #uuid "733fd798-ea86-56ea-afb5-fb25093de365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "733fd798-ea86-56ea-afb5-fb25093de365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469879} :answer-field/id #uuid "f23ba425-e844-50c7-9a2c-187594d0ae48" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470551} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49eb446a-3c97-5556-bf19-ea42b18fb478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469880} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a855ae-fa58-561d-83d1-244e26fd4609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49eb446a-3c97-5556-bf19-ea42b18fb478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469880} :answer-field/id #uuid "a564b121-378d-5751-91f3-38367384f6f0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92cb42d6-33e7-5895-a2ef-8224d17bd632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469882} {:answer/id #uuid "bde6ef7f-70fd-5236-a1cb-ae7873bad5de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92cb42d6-33e7-5895-a2ef-8224d17bd632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469882} :answer-field/id #uuid "5757eb5a-153a-5404-853e-2408f7e8d9f3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae6d946d-9a9f-5816-82c2-7048c4392f45" :question/math-academy-id "q-96857" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,-1),(-2,1),$ and $(3,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n- **I.** $(1,3)$\n- **II.** $(0,-3)$\n- **III.** $(2,3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,-9),$  $(1,3)$, and $(3,9).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \" I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33d1ca0c-c077-564f-bbd3-6bd589f331e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422351} {:answer/id #uuid "87ce1d0c-32be-5143-a872-7d49dc66b488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33d1ca0c-c077-564f-bbd3-6bd589f331e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422351} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fca4796-70aa-50d1-96e1-5e660ddb7451" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422456} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5727dd59-2f56-5c06-9b43-b63ff7c2bfb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422353} {:answer/id #uuid "842ba921-5998-5c95-bb52-17e348e3161e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "842ba921-5998-5c95-bb52-17e348e3161e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422354} :answer-field/id #uuid "658f8908-07e3-5b79-8798-c03791ed181b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422457} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b8203d5-1002-51cb-9411-d4a83fc42ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422355} {:answer/id #uuid "ad4c0de1-0610-56fb-9005-f107985bbfef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b8203d5-1002-51cb-9411-d4a83fc42ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422355} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ff5351b-54cc-5ac7-889b-b6d3ef3ffe59" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "765ad5be-eea7-5159-b982-461fb59d4587" :question/math-academy-id "q-96988" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $2x-{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$\n- **II.** $3{y}^{′}-2{e}^{x}y={y}^{2},\\,y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)=1$\n- **III.** $2x{y}^{″}-\\frac{1}{x}={y}^{′},\\,y(2)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=1$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System I  is not a first-order initial value problem. We have a first-order ordinary differential equation, but there is no initial condition.\n\n- System II is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $3{y}^{′}-2{e}^{x}y={y}^{2}$ together with the initial condition $y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)=1.$\n\n- System III is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation $2x{y}^{″}-\\frac{1}{x}={y}^{′}$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(2)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=1.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc873da1-dcb5-58cd-bcdc-f6dfaecd44eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422357} {:answer/id #uuid "aabe49eb-f60e-59a4-8e8e-b51a643069e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aabe49eb-f60e-59a4-8e8e-b51a643069e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422358} :answer-field/id #uuid "793806ab-841f-56f5-aae9-1f5aa1b28e93" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422459} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e61410e-bb7d-5fd5-a42c-93728f72a519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422359} {:answer/id #uuid "3904d9fc-81e9-58dc-b100-87ee0a13dfc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e61410e-bb7d-5fd5-a42c-93728f72a519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422359} :answer-field/id #uuid "503ea99b-8961-55e4-a7e1-ce13e2130792" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422460} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4347d9eb-3074-5e4f-bb59-94bee475caab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422361} {:answer/id #uuid "82b802ce-94eb-52a4-a016-7da0aee33a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82b802ce-94eb-52a4-a016-7da0aee33a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422362} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f981e7a-b93e-545d-9956-04d8aae8a018" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422461}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a63b835-35e3-55e6-8b41-bbb1ab5d0792" :question/math-academy-id "q-96990" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${x}^{3}{y}^{′}-\\sqrt{x}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\,y(1)=1$\n- **II.** $\\sqrt{x}{y}^{‴}-x{y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{4},\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2,\\,{y}^{″}(0)=1$\n- **III.** $\\sqrt{3}{y}^{′}-3x=2y,\\,y(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2)=1$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System I is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation ${x}^{3}{y}^{′}-\\sqrt{x}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ together with the initial condition $y(1)=1.$\n\n- System II is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *third*-order differential equation $\\sqrt{x}{y}^{‴}-x{y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{4}$ together with *three* initial conditions $y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2,$ and ${y}^{″}(0)=1.$ This is a third-order initial value problem.\n\n- System III is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $\\sqrt{3}{y}^{′}-3x=2y$ together with the initial condition $y(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2)=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050324 :topic/id #uuid "3ffd42a4-cf3d-5ec4-9be0-19d427299cac" :topic/math-academy-id 2014 :topic/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62ea197e-9076-5ec7-9c6b-fde342e50e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452287} {:answer/id #uuid "371eea84-4676-5f33-860c-9ae4e18c7064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "371eea84-4676-5f33-860c-9ae4e18c7064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452288} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3e5c9ca-6cc9-55d4-93e3-da3cb1057919" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bddeda6b-c779-5d38-b99c-7b9f7c3fd8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452289} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b2c027-6043-5549-871e-78ddef1107d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bddeda6b-c779-5d38-b99c-7b9f7c3fd8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452289} :answer-field/id #uuid "51370f87-3ad5-5a80-a161-072ee50a64dd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452992} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de3104b1-f9c6-562b-9198-a923998a0e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452291} {:answer/id #uuid "1fac6913-2157-5d65-b290-ffccbb160d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de3104b1-f9c6-562b-9198-a923998a0e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452291} :answer-field/id #uuid "e53a4dc2-d964-58e2-b05c-d5768a79a4e5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63a8e650-529a-5d09-8a67-87993316a8b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-97061" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050324 :topic/id #uuid "3ffd42a4-cf3d-5ec4-9be0-19d427299cac" :topic/math-academy-id 2014 :topic/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "463ae41e-390b-598e-ad2c-cc70f9b8b51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452293} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2a9785-fc82-5dbb-91e3-a0ed2dd4ee8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca2a9785-fc82-5dbb-91e3-a0ed2dd4ee8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452294} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc1bf5b2-a5c1-5687-973d-01d75246fa11" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c91a051-7a46-5af3-abb4-aa9f3ee447ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452295} {:answer/id #uuid "8a857a45-934f-59cb-806a-0ff39125394b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c91a051-7a46-5af3-abb4-aa9f3ee447ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452295} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e95157d-1201-5d7b-96c1-63d2f59338ce" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82668a3d-f3fe-5542-b38c-eb8caa646e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452297} {:answer/id #uuid "862c623a-d189-5525-b571-01f6a5171ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "862c623a-d189-5525-b571-01f6a5171ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452298} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a201872-4c57-5d35-8831-ed55fb963e8f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47f484a7-fae0-59b3-b230-0181ae09e78c" :question/math-academy-id "q-97064" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/9b/9ba3d1f0eebdfc82c40f36bdbe16896ca15516b623c695b72c331861955329bc.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050324 :topic/id #uuid "3ffd42a4-cf3d-5ec4-9be0-19d427299cac" :topic/math-academy-id 2014 :topic/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adfa5bb0-95dd-5e0f-a753-c9aa882957ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452299} {:answer/id #uuid "42f83495-bf79-5e40-bb79-ee3727fa8353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adfa5bb0-95dd-5e0f-a753-c9aa882957ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452299} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0a51104-0991-584c-8840-d4699e193686" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452997} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc60e2c0-d4d5-572f-9b0e-66723f21b412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452301} {:answer/id #uuid "150625a1-ee19-5f2b-8756-67d6f8188780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "150625a1-ee19-5f2b-8756-67d6f8188780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452302} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9c01461-e833-5fcb-90ac-4d72370339f7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452998} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5af27217-2702-5cd8-b3f6-5240c4009a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452303} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f2580e-b5b9-544c-bdb5-e0422c549813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6f2580e-b5b9-544c-bdb5-e0422c549813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452304} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae0a334b-94f1-5fb1-ac19-ba3fff9b5671" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "977acc9f-1a7e-5840-a4f9-507f36de32d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-97065" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/9b/9ba3d1f0eebdfc82c40f36bdbe16896ca15516b623c695b72c331861955329bc.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050324 :topic/id #uuid "3ffd42a4-cf3d-5ec4-9be0-19d427299cac" :topic/math-academy-id 2014 :topic/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db067e3e-7bda-5f89-ac04-b1307dd15481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452305} {:answer/id #uuid "22258483-ea45-5772-80af-642cced16361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db067e3e-7bda-5f89-ac04-b1307dd15481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452305} :answer-field/id #uuid "87d25a98-a59c-5918-a546-bfaab5b15f74" :answer-field/k