ield/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "875338da-f85c-5b2a-9645-5f7fb1d7affd" :question/math-academy-id "q-253466" :question/problem "Which of the following recurrence relations are first-order?\n- **I.** ${a}_{n}=4{a}_{n-1}+7$\n- **II.** ${b}_{n}={b}_{n-1}+3{b}_{n-3}$\n- **III.** ${c}_{n}=5{c}_{n-1}-2n$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The order of a recurrence relation is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${a}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${b}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-3}$ in the relation is $3.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $3.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${c}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${c}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363626 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129287 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Recurrence Relations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049519 :topic/id #uuid "fc01ef76-1fef-5e93-ace1-aec0dfa05f4a" :topic/math-academy-id 1989 :topic/title "Introduction to Recurrence Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcdef5db-ad28-5e48-8fdc-5f341b8f979a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468972} {:answer/id #uuid "6746e8ff-17d5-5051-a59e-b952d7106062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcdef5db-ad28-5e48-8fdc-5f341b8f979a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468972} :answer-field/id #uuid "acd69487-8e5b-58ff-833f-2dd60f8c1a2d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470098} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c57311b-350a-58f1-8742-99c22ce03f27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468974} {:answer/id #uuid "40f38343-7129-55ae-9219-7bbc98485bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40f38343-7129-55ae-9219-7bbc98485bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468975} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc7dc6c8-3ab6-5e7e-a234-18bfe70f5731" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470099} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0de410a-0b59-5401-846a-8200c3de9cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468976} {:answer/id #uuid "c3554d2b-841b-5e8b-a76f-4bce2722a39a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0de410a-0b59-5401-846a-8200c3de9cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468976} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a4cb17f-9ef1-5178-9bbe-d1df984e3597" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470100}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18b3d391-1187-5c01-902c-37defcaf71f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-253483" :question/problem "Which of the following recurrence relations are linear (with constant coefficients)?\n- **I.** ${a}_{n}=-n{a}_{n-1}+4{a}_{n-2}$\n- **II.** ${b}_{n}=5{b}_{n-1}-2n$\n- **III.** ${c}_{n}={c}_{n-1}^{2}-3{c}_{n-2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A recurrence relation is **linear (with constant coefficients)** if it expresses ${a}_{n}$ as a sum of previous terms ${a}_{n-1},…,{a}_{n-k}$ with constant coefficients, together with possibly a final term that depends only on $n:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={s}_{1}{a}_{n-1}+{s}_{2}{a}_{n-2}+…+{s}_{k}{a}_{n-k}+g(n)\n$$\n\nwhere ${s}_{1},{s}_{2},…,{s}_{k}$ are constants and $g(n)$ is a function, often called a **forcing function**, that does not involve ${a}_{n}$ or its preceding terms. \n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- ${a}_{n}$ is not linear. The coefficient of the term $-n{a}_{n-1}$ is not constant.\n\n- ${b}_{n}$ is linear. The term ${b}_{n-1}$ occurs only in the first power with constant coefficient.\n\n- ${c}_{n}$ is not linear. The term ${c}_{n-1}^{2}$ is not in the first power.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129287 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Recurrence Relations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049519 :topic/id #uuid "fc01ef76-1fef-5e93-ace1-aec0dfa05f4a" :topic/math-academy-id 1989 :topic/title "Introduction to Recurrence Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd5000ba-a84e-5f4f-8e78-62c27fcef410" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468978} {:answer/id #uuid "54724c17-9b61-5b68-afa2-274eeaede92e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd5000ba-a84e-5f4f-8e78-62c27fcef410" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468978} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e8af14e-48e4-56c6-bd08-eaebb65b255e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4db00c4-1f0b-5a38-919a-e635a62442dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468980} {:answer/id #uuid "b081acba-51e2-5ff4-9ca1-880a90f9c71d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b081acba-51e2-5ff4-9ca1-880a90f9c71d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468981} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c8e5b18-c2aa-5345-b421-40be0bc32242" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49389e30-ccc1-56fc-b53d-0859e211257c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468982} {:answer/id #uuid "1d086ae5-7568-5f7d-bd78-535c42b2dc41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49389e30-ccc1-56fc-b53d-0859e211257c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468982} :answer-field/id #uuid "eab85fd6-2621-5f8b-8c8b-18c59a408929" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c27291fe-59f1-5d75-bef8-47b51d3e493f" :question/math-academy-id "q-253486" :question/problem "Which of the following linear recurrence relations are homogeneous?\n- **I.** ${a}_{n}={a}_{n-1}-3{a}_{n-2}+n$\n- **II.** ${b}_{n}={b}_{n-1}+5{b}_{n-2}$\n- **III.** ${c}_{n}=6{c}_{n-1}+1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A linear recurrence relation (with constant coefficients) is **homogeneous** if the forcing function is zero. \n\nIn other words, the linear recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={s}_{1}{a}_{n-1}+{s}_{2}{a}_{n-2}+…+{s}_{k}{a}_{n-k}+g(n),\n$$\n\nis homogeneous if $g(n)=0$ for all $n,$ and ${s}_{i}$ is constant for each $i.$\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- ${a}_{n}$ is not homogeneous. The term $n$ of the expression doesn't contain preceding terms of the relation.\n\n- ${b}_{n}$ is homogeneous. The terms of the expression each contain a preceding term, ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}.$\n\n- ${c}_{n}$ is not homogeneous. The term $1$ of the expression doesn't contain preceding terms of the relation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363640 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129287 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Recurrence Relations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049519 :topic/id #uuid "fc01ef76-1fef-5e93-ace1-aec0dfa05f4a" :topic/math-academy-id 1989 :topic/title "Introduction to Recurrence Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82a1a307-f88b-5ae2-b5f3-698480fb3a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468984} {:answer/id #uuid "d82b1b53-9c2d-5039-9960-a0f426d40b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82a1a307-f88b-5ae2-b5f3-698480fb3a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468984} :answer-field/id #uuid "be5ee870-2911-520a-a1a3-3b517a71e897" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae940a50-faf7-5e76-8c24-8ee2b38c3e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468986} {:answer/id #uuid "a517f42e-0b1f-5486-909d-b50ad6589830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a517f42e-0b1f-5486-909d-b50ad6589830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468987} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb3c42c2-942b-5f73-a85b-a91ae6839072" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12868c2e-01d5-5b4e-905a-bf03d3bfe271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468988} {:answer/id #uuid "84471fd6-5b8e-5c99-bfb2-bbefaacdfe96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84471fd6-5b8e-5c99-bfb2-bbefaacdfe96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468989} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ac54eee-eb91-5ed4-8952-66790e801e40" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8e46c1db-beb9-52c4-8f72-f2f2edfce45c" :question/math-academy-id "q-253487" :question/problem "Which of the following linear recurrence relations are homogeneous?\n- **I.** ${a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{3}{a}_{n-1}-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n-2}+2$\n- **II.** ${b}_{n}=5{b}_{n-1}-{b}_{n-2}$\n- **III.** ${c}_{n}=\\frac{1}{4}{c}_{n-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A linear recurrence relation (with constant coefficients) is **homogeneous** if the forcing function is zero. \n\nIn other words, the linear recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={s}_{1}{a}_{n-1}+{s}_{2}{a}_{n-2}+…+{s}_{k}{a}_{n-k}+g(n),\n$$\n\nis homogeneous if $g(n)=0$ for all $n,$ and ${s}_{i}$ is constant for each $i.$\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- ${a}_{n}$ is not homogeneous. The term $2$ of the expression doesn't contain preceding terms of the relation.\n\n- ${b}_{n}$ is homogeneous. The terms of the expression each contain a preceding term, ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}.$\n\n- ${c}_{n}$ is homogeneous. The term of the expression contains a preceding term, ${c}_{n-1}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364040 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28939f65-9fd6-564d-a0c2-73c1038ac898" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous and Inhomogeneous Systems" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048451 :topic/id #uuid "a0acd569-aa75-5c03-9c8e-bc8f5d31d263" :topic/math-academy-id 2086 :topic/title "Introduction to Systems of Linear ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6274ca14-71b7-584e-9fad-627e6bb3647b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469002} {:answer/id #uuid "2130c5ff-c6dc-5430-bd8b-cc474d561b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6274ca14-71b7-584e-9fad-627e6bb3647b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469002} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5289ed2-c3f8-57e6-b594-24d7b19e3206" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a0088c9-d855-5d3c-abe4-57fc9b510b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469004} {:answer/id #uuid "4416a39f-3a6f-5252-80e1-3ca08bc5515c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a0088c9-d855-5d3c-abe4-57fc9b510b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469004} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8fa675f-42d1-5003-b1f6-4f19b3be9fba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88c5e74f-4d70-5387-b323-a08f8ffc808b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469006} {:answer/id #uuid "456e0360-717e-58ed-a6a9-d455c5010e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "456e0360-717e-58ed-a6a9-d455c5010e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469007} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cf16879-ef9f-5dde-81f2-198d6428c199" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1ece1ec-19c9-5790-a759-998564647939" :question/math-academy-id "q-339659" :question/problem "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n- **I.** ${x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** ${x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **III.** ${x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "In matrix form, the system\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=A(t)x(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nis *homogeneous* when $f≡0,$ and *inhomogeneous* when $f≢0.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is inhomogeneous since $f=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}≢0.$\n\n- System II is inhomogeneous since $f=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}≢0.$\n\n- System III is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28939f65-9fd6-564d-a0c2-73c1038ac898" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous and Inhomogeneous Systems" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048451 :topic/id #uuid "a0acd569-aa75-5c03-9c8e-bc8f5d31d263" :topic/math-academy-id 2086 :topic/title "Introduction to Systems of Linear ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991120bc-4c7f-5c42-86d8-269fd66049fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469008} {:answer/id #uuid "e67a8af1-e73d-5edd-9eff-117cb8b7302c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e67a8af1-e73d-5edd-9eff-117cb8b7302c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469009} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b0bc8f9-87ac-58f1-84d0-9d35a22fd5ca" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc24f97d-cfa8-51ec-8c51-a0756938234f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469010} {:answer/id #uuid "2b7e858a-8dde-5fc2-bba2-3e14b58bcf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc24f97d-cfa8-51ec-8c51-a0756938234f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469010} :answer-field/id #uuid "d40aa99e-e178-5ad6-ac3e-3ca49e4e191e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7609147f-db98-571c-8ae6-0e50f9304600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469012} {:answer/id #uuid "46d76a06-c329-51f3-ad5f-24933501ead9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46d76a06-c329-51f3-ad5f-24933501ead9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469013} :answer-field/id #uuid "53cdcdbe-8b4c-52b2-807e-bcd1f8888a3d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73f3b368-2531-52b2-833e-f683b0622933" :question/math-academy-id "q-339665" :question/problem "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n- **I.** $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n- **II.** $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-2{x}_{1}(t)+5\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n- **III.** $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=7{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of the form\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIf $f≡0$ and $g≡0$ (i.e., both $f$ and $g$ are zero functions), then the system is *homogeneous*. Otherwise, if at least one of $f$ or $g$ is not identically zero, the system is *inhomogeneous*.\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=3, &  & b(t)=2, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=-1, &  & d(t)=4, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $g≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=-1, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=-2, &  & d(t)=0, &  & g(t)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System III is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=0, &  & b(t)=0, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=7, &  & d(t)=3, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "113a601e-220a-54a3-a64b-1e554bc3d79f" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049371 :topic/id #uuid "ef6bb570-cff7-5ef3-a4ba-79063f5d81ad" :topic/math-academy-id 1962 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfe45e96-b6f2-5280-bd02-15325098a1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469032} {:answer/id #uuid "d1208062-b192-5bb7-a768-32fe16db1321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfe45e96-b6f2-5280-bd02-15325098a1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469032} :answer-field/id #uuid "01a567c0-0023-5025-af7d-e7a0249210c8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e99694d5-15bf-5e3c-9954-8af1c80b4a01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469034} {:answer/id #uuid "427ca074-860f-5ae5-b4a1-3f89a485e8d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e99694d5-15bf-5e3c-9954-8af1c80b4a01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469034} :answer-field/id #uuid "338eec5c-2406-5f0c-bb1c-c1531ce433f3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470129} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64b50964-d370-5d75-8291-5c06aa29eca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469036} {:answer/id #uuid "7af62786-7b5e-59ed-ad41-57aa0b2131b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7af62786-7b5e-59ed-ad41-57aa0b2131b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469037} :answer-field/id #uuid "912585d5-f1a5-5f2d-97a9-471dd9c27ba3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e3fcd83b-c9bf-54f3-97b2-1811800f0c15" :question/math-academy-id "q-38889" :question/problem "Let $T:{R}^{7}\\to {R}^{7}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If ${v}_{1}\\ne {v}_{2}$ vectors such that $T({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\}$\n- **II.** $T$ is invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{7}$ into ${R}^{7},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{7} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=7 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$\n\nSince $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\nT({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})\\,⟹\\,T({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since ${v}_{1}-{v}_{2}\\in \\text{Ker}(T)$ and ${v}_{1}\\ne {v}_{2},$ we must have that $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne \\{0\\},$ the transformation $T$ and the matrix $T$ are not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0.$ In turn, this means that $\\text{nullity}(T)>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "113a601e-220a-54a3-a64b-1e554bc3d79f" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049371 :topic/id #uuid "ef6bb570-cff7-5ef3-a4ba-79063f5d81ad" :topic/math-academy-id 1962 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae1d25d6-8ed3-59df-911c-7d0cb3fdc8ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469044} {:answer/id #uuid "5ceb7842-8979-5416-aad4-760e628285f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ceb7842-8979-5416-aad4-760e628285f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469045} :answer-field/id #uuid "e42f00c6-6c84-5fb6-8df5-83a524e29e2c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21598207-e841-5f39-8f2a-4ec2cfbec0fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469046} {:answer/id #uuid "c901c73f-ddc2-5d19-aeaa-5345c49b20f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21598207-e841-5f39-8f2a-4ec2cfbec0fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469046} :answer-field/id #uuid "e45cb722-742a-5576-a0d9-c95cfa6bdb62" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470135} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74ba564d-eeea-5879-b8d0-f329022e980d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469048} {:answer/id #uuid "2b4543b5-7c0b-5482-af32-ce6dac305545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74ba564d-eeea-5879-b8d0-f329022e980d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469048} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c7852e2-0fb8-517d-a85f-e3a3e578317a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3c1b6231-ddc6-5ac3-a5c8-9d11b32158e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-47456" :question/problem "Let $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T,$ and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(T).$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If ${v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}+{v}_{3}=0$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0$\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(T)=3$\n- **III.** $T$ is a bijection\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{3}$ into ${R}^{3},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=3 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since the columns of $T$ satisfies ${v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}+{v}_{3}=0$, then they are linearly dependent, which gives us $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Col}(T)\\ne {R}^{3}.$ Therefore, according to the Invertible Matrix Theorem, we must have $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{3}$, then $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{3},$ the transformation $T$ can't be a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049371 :topic/id #uuid "ef6bb570-cff7-5ef3-a4ba-79063f5d81ad" :topic/math-academy-id 1962 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations"} :activity/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490508} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491234}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26bd6f4b-2b75-5c2f-af4a-69dc991cef5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574529} {:answer/id #uuid "19aec9f4-1be6-57e6-acd8-0eb7a0bced1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26bd6f4b-2b75-5c2f-af4a-69dc991cef5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574529} :answer-field/id #uuid "fca21163-dca5-5a67-95c2-b5c65a7a79d6" :answer-field/key "Column 1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574747} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63d24914-88dc-51e2-81f3-dd8fa6d63228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574531} {:answer/id #uuid "a4969d2e-b3bc-58f8-a692-40817c328144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63d24914-88dc-51e2-81f3-dd8fa6d63228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574531} :answer-field/id #uuid "576de36d-7da0-5474-bf94-4879338dda25" :answer-field/key "Column 2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9d93eca-6b3e-5248-b23c-b4860f340f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574533} {:answer/id #uuid "6c399d0b-63f0-570a-b733-9ba3a1cb7a01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c399d0b-63f0-570a-b733-9ba3a1cb7a01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574534} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b60e5e0-8c33-5e92-9773-9494b4cbfdf7" :answer-field/key "Column 3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574749} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b1bacd-225d-5252-b0c7-3bc575b87f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574535} {:answer/id #uuid "c8aa4f44-f064-5ef7-8cd7-b782dc4aff92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05b1bacd-225d-5252-b0c7-3bc575b87f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574535} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dfee52c-e9e8-5fe9-91f9-c2bbff64a284" :answer-field/key "Column 4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5149a8bf-4216-5b0c-825e-8103ee48f823" :question/math-academy-id "q-73621" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $R$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $R$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445 :topic/id #uuid "a01c36d3-5643-5685-845e-29c37e89238f" :topic/math-academy-id 1733 :topic/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e2d5a83-8718-5bdf-8eb3-db892e2ab5e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438532} {:answer/id #uuid "8eaaea36-3739-5e8a-a1ed-efc15f9bc00b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e2d5a83-8718-5bdf-8eb3-db892e2ab5e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438532} :answer-field/id #uuid "8efd7542-c77b-5d4d-8f60-5468e0925423" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439295} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "763f0363-fe65-5380-acc8-6965de771643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438534} {:answer/id #uuid "be014b12-0b58-51d7-a7a3-d343e4554293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be014b12-0b58-51d7-a7a3-d343e4554293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438535} :answer-field/id #uuid "1338d41d-dfae-54bb-ada6-b58b1d8cc303" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439296} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f48fb77e-36ef-5915-aaab-7df2660d984a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438536} {:answer/id #uuid "84b40478-f69c-539e-aac5-dd183a05b951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f48fb77e-36ef-5915-aaab-7df2660d984a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438536} :answer-field/id #uuid "7051a40c-c2de-5375-95a6-8801b39f67c5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35b0295d-1e16-59cc-a201-696e791e0b7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74643" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=8 \\\\ x+y &=-2 \\\\ x+\\frac{1}{2}y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system has no solution\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=-2 \\\\ -y &=14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-14.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-14)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=12.\n$$\n\n \nSo,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent.   \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133864 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1304189f-61ac-53c5-9b09-8e365f763136" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Factors in a QR Factorization" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050130 :topic/id #uuid "2f232786-4262-5d64-9c58-1578e8c629d2" :topic/math-academy-id 2129 :topic/title "QR Factorization"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0346398f-65b8-5bd3-b0f9-8b628f52a353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452221} {:answer/id #uuid "bceb1ecc-febc-5631-a278-5aed524c28fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bceb1ecc-febc-5631-a278-5aed524c28fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452222} :answer-field/id #uuid "97cbf390-2de4-5d0c-9c7a-49c1601d1072" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452958} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3b4bd9b-5b77-560c-a577-20bdb4c3f47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452223} {:answer/id #uuid "dedc586f-9e2a-5d88-add5-529a718afa93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dedc586f-9e2a-5d88-add5-529a718afa93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452224} :answer-field/id #uuid "e78d5e63-ee82-56c8-9657-4763f39441dd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452959} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c92a537c-38be-543f-9b04-f1d82d249904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452225} {:answer/id #uuid "e48f546a-1da8-5e18-b960-859e9f202044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e48f546a-1da8-5e18-b960-859e9f202044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452226} :answer-field/id #uuid "120438b3-dec2-597e-a996-fd9ef95e4b98" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14a18e20-8a94-54a8-afff-0a503b7d967c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95916" :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The columns of $Q$ are orthonormal\n\n- **II.** $Q$ is a square matrix\n\n- **III.** $R$ is a square matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis, they are orthonormal.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $Q$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix, it is square.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $R$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix, it is square.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133864 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1304189f-61ac-53c5-9b09-8e365f763136" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Factors in a QR Factorization" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050130 :topic/id #uuid "2f232786-4262-5d64-9c58-1578e8c629d2" :topic/math-academy-id 2129 :topic/title "QR Factorization"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa96bbef-e60b-5938-afd9-9aecce3662a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452227} {:answer/id #uuid "fc82ac14-9f60-5ff5-abf6-9be439d5811c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa96bbef-e60b-5938-afd9-9aecce3662a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452227} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fe0a7f0-668f-540b-a54e-2bb0427d1d40" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0037e982-4e96-568d-9977-84d06128905e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452229} {:answer/id #uuid "72d0b427-e976-5eed-8e23-5bc0a65dd9f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72d0b427-e976-5eed-8e23-5bc0a65dd9f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452230} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f6a5e16-c6e0-5de3-b5c7-56166731c92b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452962} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ffe0134-9e43-5357-bfb9-2d702d98cc8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452231} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4c660a-4b11-554a-9592-b3bbc7fe081e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa4c660a-4b11-554a-9592-b3bbc7fe081e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452232} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d9d8be5-9c71-5d23-9c41-8e0eb84f478a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2d40cdd9-dee2-5236-bb35-1c36eb46fb25" :question/math-academy-id "q-95922" :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $4\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $Q$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** $R$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n- **III.** The columns of $Q$ are orthonormal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a  QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. $Q$ should be a $4\\times 2$ matrix, so it is not square.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, $R$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis, $Q$ must be an orthogonal matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ca319c5-9f62-51e3-b670-611fc8a8daaa" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Critical Point Using the Second Partial Derivatives Test" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051048 :topic/id #uuid "7d157e41-c50b-570b-8b5b-b8a5a0d03163" :topic/math-academy-id 1944 :topic/title "The Second Partial Derivatives Test"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62cbcaa0-0a4b-5073-ad88-c02a4ba1a019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451299} {:answer/id #uuid "375e98ca-c238-53ff-beba-897b64cc63a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62cbcaa0-0a4b-5073-ad88-c02a4ba1a019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451299} :answer-field/id #uuid "652213cb-11aa-5dea-a4bc-3b9c8b1c355c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452497} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b0d48c5-2f2c-5055-908e-0dc95f5f7282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451301} {:answer/id #uuid "61b6f0c7-25e4-5be3-b321-0d0f90827d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61b6f0c7-25e4-5be3-b321-0d0f90827d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451302} :answer-field/id #uuid "d71cb01d-fa4d-51c3-8af9-10186ba20c84" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452498} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd7d602-b04e-508c-8f43-638a3bb96a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451303} {:answer/id #uuid "cafd6976-b47f-5881-a12d-13755ea64993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cafd6976-b47f-5881-a12d-13755ea64993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451304} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a57395c-fb2f-5e27-af13-56da5d453d17" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2adfa73-7e18-5d5d-8163-694e5efa8a14" :question/math-academy-id "q-104980" :question/problem "The function $f(x,y)$ has Hessian matrix\n\n$$\n{∇}^{2}f(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2}+2(y-3) & 2(x+1) \\\\ 2(x+1) & (y-3)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(-1,3).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $H(-1,3)<0$\n- **II.** $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(-1,3)>0$\n- **III.** The second partial derivative test is inconclusive" :question/worked-solution "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ then:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$;\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a.$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a.$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivative test is inconclusive.\n\nEvaluating the Hessian at $(-1,3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{∇}^{2}f(-1,3)=\\begin{bmatrix}(-1)^{2}+2(3-3) & 2(-1+1) \\\\ 2(-1+1) & (3-3)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The Hessian determinant is\n\n$$\nH(-1,3)=det({∇}^{2}f(-1,3))=1(0)-0(0)=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true because\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(-1,3)=1>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true because $H(-1,3)=0,$ so the second partial derivative test is inconclusive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aee17e3a-031d-5c0e-9488-17410b3a2372" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Dimensions of Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049808 :topic/id #uuid "15638861-fef2-549b-9318-e9b1cdad2ec4" :topic/math-academy-id 2759 :topic/title "Dimension in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54cbfca0-bff0-52dc-a7d3-f7f9ea5acb20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468858} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8db7bb-912a-549b-8dc7-d4e68d879053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab8db7bb-912a-549b-8dc7-d4e68d879053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468859} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc9b4d17-b28a-526f-8892-83a499708178" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470041} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c5112c1-4747-5e8b-a12b-430126d5ce9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468860} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8614be-f12e-5507-b395-aa4a960dd2ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c5112c1-4747-5e8b-a12b-430126d5ce9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468860} :answer-field/id #uuid "e370841a-5acd-57e5-9802-a92d25d0133e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae1bff07-aba3-5a99-aece-07d510737e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468862} {:answer/id #uuid "1a402636-9d56-5283-8679-8961a991afe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae1bff07-aba3-5a99-aece-07d510737e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468862} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea2f7538-5026-507b-a35a-db7e12ed1e93" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a2340ea-4d69-565f-a0a6-1a2327573430" :question/math-academy-id "q-106904" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $11?$\n- **I.** ${R}_{10}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $10$\n- **II.** ${\\text{M}}_{2\\times 6}(R),$ the vector space of all $2\\times 6$ matrices over $R$\n- **III.** ${R}^{10}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{10}[t])=10+1=11.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{2\\times 6}(R))=2\\cdot 6=12\\ne 11.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{10})=10\\ne 11.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152221 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e609aabf-7e7e-5997-b8dc-c66e7a14a36f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Finite and Infinite-Dimensional Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049808 :topic/id #uuid "15638861-fef2-549b-9318-e9b1cdad2ec4" :topic/math-academy-id 2759 :topic/title "Dimension in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de766be9-7744-5bfb-8b2f-8023fc3158cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468864} {:answer/id #uuid "2f125859-37a5-5537-ba48-6d2ee36d6bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de766be9-7744-5bfb-8b2f-8023fc3158cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468864} :answer-field/id #uuid "6be09d3c-75d8-5d3d-919f-3773c54a4af7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5af34f65-86e0-5151-8a15-9503bee30c18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468866} {:answer/id #uuid "0fb68f23-b130-57cd-a680-8d96d33d7e7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fb68f23-b130-57cd-a680-8d96d33d7e7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468867} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfc19938-334a-52b1-a436-771c8fabe642" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13b3e34b-7482-55bd-b20d-64ca8e7437bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468868} {:answer/id #uuid "93ae5df4-23d2-523c-b530-f71615d60fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93ae5df4-23d2-523c-b530-f71615d60fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468869} :answer-field/id #uuid "e613ab11-478a-590d-a0b0-981f9038f46d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ad8a280-94c8-5978-909a-9e22277ca8ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-106918" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n- **I.** $D(R),$ the vector space of all differentiable functions on $R$\n- **II.** ${R}^{100}$\n- **III.** ${R}_{2000}[t],$ the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2\\,000$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- $D(R)$ is *not* finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following subset of $D(R)$ is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,{t}^{n}},\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{x}_{i}{t}^{i}=0\n$$\n\nfor all $t\\in R$ if and only if ${x}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of $D(R)$  of size $n,$ which imples that $D(R)$ cannot have finite dimension.     .\n\n- ${R}^{100}$ and ${R}_{2000}[t]$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{100})=100\n$$\n\n \nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{2000}[t])=2000+1=2\\,001,\n$$\n\nare both finite numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172029 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a6bbb34-a43f-5e16-8a24-25c0d6970a38" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Curve Type From Its Reduced Equation: No Cross-Product Term" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050760 :topic/id #uuid "64670a5e-dd35-51fc-bd24-210590f74fcd" :topic/math-academy-id 3336 :topic/title "Classifying Quadratic Curves"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86538b9a-7568-5933-8854-c5b4658f48fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468942} {:answer/id #uuid "7015220a-f9e7-5df7-8058-44ffcd7f8d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7015220a-f9e7-5df7-8058-44ffcd7f8d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468943} :answer-field/id #uuid "1042346b-f6d0-5bb9-9f5f-bce0a807b4a3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470083} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec93fa16-4cde-5228-9add-72224548a4b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468944} {:answer/id #uuid "f37fedd9-c61b-5bc4-9e9b-a9572e1053ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f37fedd9-c61b-5bc4-9e9b-a9572e1053ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468945} :answer-field/id #uuid "862e7db4-e4cf-5fa7-beaa-ce2dadf572fd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470084} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8f6328b-6e1c-5742-b270-297de5ba0087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468946} {:answer/id #uuid "3f2783d8-30e3-52a0-8485-391ca3a4046f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f2783d8-30e3-52a0-8485-391ca3a4046f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468947} :answer-field/id #uuid "b91acfa1-f88a-5755-910e-8b8e92796d63" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7ec5e81-6115-5881-b6f7-16bb9226da5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-140554" :question/problem "Which of the following equations define a non-empty set of points in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane?\n- **I.** ${x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}=-1$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}=0$\n- **III.** ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the equations in turn.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}=-1$ defines a non-empty set. It represents the hyperbola ${x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2}=1.$\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}=0$ defines a non-empty set. It represents a parabola that opens in the direction of the negative ${x}_{2}$-axis in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=0$ defines a non-empty set. It represents a single point $(0,0)$ in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162013 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c67d532-acd9-5231-a27f-d39084863e01" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Spectral Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049849 :topic/id #uuid "1887f465-a1b8-5370-82f6-80e02b9d153a" :topic/math-academy-id 3120 :topic/title "The Spectral Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb7dde31-bde1-58e8-ad71-ec6b2e8b2319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451311} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca9aaad-54c8-5fad-9a03-14113c01dc8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb7dde31-bde1-58e8-ad71-ec6b2e8b2319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451311} :answer-field/id #uuid "e741fb79-46a4-593a-9d56-3df9c7384c94" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452503} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05cc96c4-9bd0-5ec2-9c67-70c12fe56748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451313} {:answer/id #uuid "71be77cb-f2a0-5da9-a71b-0d54bf22920e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05cc96c4-9bd0-5ec2-9c67-70c12fe56748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451313} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fda6962-d111-5d52-9d97-94bb5cf1b992" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452504} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "757e1e41-d4bd-5b02-ae6c-09acb0b026a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451315} {:answer/id #uuid "ae88a715-f3a8-55f4-890a-5a6165ebc0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae88a715-f3a8-55f4-890a-5a6165ebc0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451316} :answer-field/id #uuid "c19a4f3d-993f-546f-aa3d-c187f50b1a7a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb8cc465-a001-5ad5-bfcd-11eb17855f11" :question/math-academy-id "q-140844" :question/problem "Given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ real symmetric matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is not diagonalizable\n- **II.** $A$ must have $4$ integer eigenvalues\n- **III.** If  $\\alpha $ is an eigenvalue of $A$ with the multiplicity $2,$ then the dimension of the eigenspace for the eigenvalue $\\alpha $ is $2.$" :question/worked-solution "Given that $A$ is an $n\\times n$ symmetric matrix over $R$, the spectral theorem states the following:\n\n- The eigenvalues of $A$ are all real.\n\n- Eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues are orthogonal.\n\n- The dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n\n- $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the spectral theorem, any symmetric matrix with real entries is orthogonally diagonalizable, so, $A$ is diagonalizable.\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the spectral theorem, the eigenvalues are real but not necessarily integers.\n\n- Statement III is true. According to the theorem, the dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049849 :topic/id #uuid "1887f465-a1b8-5370-82f6-80e02b9d153a" :topic/math-academy-id 3120 :topic/title "The Spectral Theorem"} :activity/title "The Spectral Theorem" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544069} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544908}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050021 :topic/id #uuid "268943d4-aaa4-5e39-9db5-48d7523acdc3" :topic/math-academy-id 3118 :topic/title "Symmetric Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8b08f7a-3777-5f1a-a9eb-461a2fd0414f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451335} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1dc0f1-cd98-5509-9477-51d011494a2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8b08f7a-3777-5f1a-a9eb-461a2fd0414f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451335} :answer-field/id #uuid "57869de9-6ee9-5e0b-90f9-6810fc1f801e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452515} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c06a9fc-e9e1-5f78-abd6-96a1dabad6e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451337} {:answer/id #uuid "e431efe4-4133-5a40-bbcf-62064ac9644b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e431efe4-4133-5a40-bbcf-62064ac9644b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451338} :answer-field/id #uuid "308a1332-e85b-5404-b4a5-ba01221b22ad" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452516} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9313834d-4423-5042-bc49-9390326be415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451339} {:answer/id #uuid "28ce3ebb-bcf9-5d61-a603-60625891c0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28ce3ebb-bcf9-5d61-a603-60625891c0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451340} :answer-field/id #uuid "237be3da-ec76-5d1e-936e-544f31cdde31" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b742394a-cffb-5df9-9fbd-181d0debffeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-143683" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** If $A$ is *any* matrix, then ${A}^{3}$ is always symmetric.\n- **II.** The sum of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n- **III.** The difference of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nHowever, ${A}^{3}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}-{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A-B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166896 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "276898e7-57a4-5ca6-8df7-99fd318a2702" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Decoupled System of Linear ODEs" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049852 :topic/id #uuid "18c7c8d4-f8df-5ab7-94e4-a5bda9fa7a9b" :topic/math-academy-id 3238 :topic/title "Solving Decoupled Homogeneous Systems of ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79e6baab-1808-5120-89bc-116fafa9f74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468990} {:answer/id #uuid "eac07d78-a7a2-5dfe-87f8-a01eb434d336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79e6baab-1808-5120-89bc-116fafa9f74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468990} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9d469c8-f695-5993-8677-034696487b48" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "651ce891-22e2-516c-b4a5-bd76f0bcbe50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468992} {:answer/id #uuid "55ec1ca4-ad6c-5c25-80f7-7ac997155c9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55ec1ca4-ad6c-5c25-80f7-7ac997155c9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468993} :answer-field/id #uuid "b900a48f-0d45-549e-8e13-96a10ba611f3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470108} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6f9fb71-005c-56c6-8fb5-6322448b76b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468994} {:answer/id #uuid "3de14d47-3e28-5e31-9272-df20e765bff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6f9fb71-005c-56c6-8fb5-6322448b76b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468994} :answer-field/id #uuid "701a6699-3227-552c-aecd-c57986c59c5d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1bf4017-8b21-55a6-92c8-e49841f3879b" :question/math-academy-id "q-331092" :question/problem "Which of the following systems of linear ODEs are decoupled?\n- **I.** ${x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x(t)$\n- **II.** ${x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}x(t)$\n- **III.** ${x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *decoupled system* consists of equations depending on only one variable, such as\n\n$$\n{x}_{i}^{′}(t)={\\lambda }_{i}{x}_{i}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\lambda }_{i}$ is a constant. This means that we can solve each equation independently.  \n\nIn matrix form, a linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ is decoupled if $A$ is a diagonal matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our systems.\n\n- System II is decoupled since its corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n\n- Systems I and III are *not* decoupled because their matrices are not diagonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}]
